I spent my morning in a college lecture and my afternoon writing production code.

Being a 20-year-old student-founder in Bangalore means living in two different worlds at the same time. During the day, I am sitting in class trying to pay attention to academic theory.

During the breaks, I am opening my laptop in the corridor to work. My friends are planning where to hang out after class, while I am worrying about product shipping delays.

It gets exhausting sometimes, tbh. But there is a weird kind of rush in applying what you learn in real-time to your own work.

Building Prettiva & Co. while managing assignments forces me to be incredibly disciplined with my calendar. I do not have time for perfect plans, I just have to ship code and fix things on the fly.

How did you manage your schedule when you were first starting out in your career?

#studentfounder #bangalore #startup
